        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-918",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "scan_url(url) passes the entry-point parameter `url` directly and unvalidated into _http_get(url), which urlparses it and opens an http.client.HTTPSConnection to whatever host/scheme the caller supplies, then issues conn.request('GET', path_and_query) against it -- a classic SSRF: any caller of scan_url (e.g. a service that lets users submit a model URL to scan) can make the server issue outbound requests to arbitrary hosts/ports (e.g. internal/metadata services), with no allow-list or validation of scheme/host.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Verified directly against source and graph. scan_url(url) (scanner.py:625-628) forwards the caller-supplied `url` straight into _http_get(url) with zero validation. _http_get (scanner.py:250-269) does `urllib.parse.urlparse(url)` then unconditionally opens `http.client.HTTPSConnection(parsed_url.netloc)` and issues `conn.request(\"GET\", path_and_query)` \u2014 there is no allow-list, scheme check, or host/IP restriction anywhere in the method (confirmed by listing every CpgCall in lines 250-270: only logging, parsing, string-building, the connection/request, and redirect-follow/error-raise calls \u2014 no validation call exists). A 302 response is even auto-followed (line 262) by recursing into _http_get with the attacker/redirect-supplied Location header, so an SSRF can also be reached via an intermediate redirect. The graph independently confirms reachability: EntryPoint 'src/picklescan/scanner.py:<module>.scan_url' has exposure=reachable/kind=handler, and the `_http_get(url)` CpgCall at line 628 (uid 8611ddd710ae66de052eb82eafdd1c4566252afa) has reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=1 \u2014 so this is not a graph-under-linking edge case, it is a directly reachable, flagged-reachable sink. cli.py:65-66 also shows the function is exposed to end users via `-u/--url`, and any embedding application (e.g. a web service letting users submit a model URL to scan, as the picklescan README documents) that forwards user input to scan_url would let that user make the server connect to arbitrary internal/external hosts and ports with no restriction. This is a genuine CWE-918 SSRF."
          },
